- provenance: inferred

## Operation: RunCommunication

### Summary

The backend runs a communication: a quick send, an automation run by hand or at a scheduled time, or the automations of a system event that happened.

### Input

```schema
communicationId: string ref(juicebar.communications#Communication.id)
channel: string required
recipients: list(part(juicebar.communications#Recipient))
subject: string
template: string
active: boolean required
organisationId: string ref(juicebar.core#Organisation.id)
userId: string
event: string
```

### Ensures

- An inactive communication is not run; otherwise a task carries out the run and keeps its progress — [mutates](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:TaskQueue), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[RUN])
- Each recipient's provider gives its addresses and the data for the placeholders, among the organisation's customers — [invokes](aim:juicebar.communications#Capability:RecipientProviders), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[PROVIDERS])
- Each address gets the subject and text with their placeholders filled, through the channel, and the result is kept — [invokes](aim:juicebar.communications#Capability:MessageDelivery), [mutates](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:DeliveryResult), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[RUN]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[CHANNELS])
- A history entry records the run and whether it was done or failed — [mutates](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:HistoryEntry), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[RUN])
- A failed delivery, or a failed run started by an event, is announced unless that event was itself a failed delivery — [emits](aim:juicebar.communications#Event:EmailSendFailed), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[RUN])
- A stored communication's count goes up by one — [mutates](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Communication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[RUN])
- The automations whose event names a system event that happened run with that event's data — [reads](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Communication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[EVENTRUN])

### Returns

- The id of the task that carries out the run.

### Bindings

- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/components/SendingCommunicationProcess.ts#SendingCommunicationProcess` — as: handler
- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/modules/Communications.ts#Communications.processCommunicationEvent` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Event: EmailSendFailed

### Summary

A delivery of a run failed, or a run started by an event failed, with the data the message was filled from and the reason, "Sending mail failed." followed by the error.

### Payload

```schema
failMessage: string required
```

### Routing

- Channel: email_send_failed

### Bindings

- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/components/SendingCommunicationProcess.ts#SendingCommunicationProcess` — as: topic
- provenance: inferred

## Record: Communication

### Summary

One automation: a communication kept to run again.

### Schema

```schema
id: string required unique
name: string
key: string
active: boolean
event: string
channel: string
content: string
subject: string
recipients: list(part(juicebar.communications#Recipient))
count: integer
scheduledTimestamps: list(part(juicebar.communications#ScheduledTime))
organisation_id: string ref(juicebar.core#Organisation.id)
```

### Constraints

- `event` is the key of an event of the `communications` configuration, and `channel` the key of a channel.
- `content` holds a content's id; nothing stops that content being deleted. A communication another module makes for itself may hold its text there instead, with its subject in `subject` and a `key` naming it.
- `active` is on from the start for the events Manual communication and Scheduled communications, and off for any other event or none.
- `count` is the number of times it ran.

### Bindings

- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/models/Communication.ts#Communication` — as: model
- provenance: inferred

## Record: Recipient

### Summary

One recipient of a communication: a recipient provider with its parameters.

### Schema

```schema
id: string
ref: string required
params: string
inputType: enum(customer_list, customer_group, event_params, attributes_filter, form_customers, firebase_customer_list)
parameter: enum(email, wallet, phone)
customerIDs: list(string)
```

### Constraints

- `ref` is a provider's key and `params` the text its selection type (`inputType`) builds. A quick send's recipient holds `ref` and `params` alone.
- `customerIDs` holds the ids of the customers chosen in a customer list or form customers. Customers are not modelled, so they name no Record.

### Bindings

- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/types/CommunicationProcessParameters.ts#CommunicationRecipient` — as: model
- provenance: inferred

## Record: ScheduledTime

### Summary

A time an automation was scheduled to run at.

### Schema

```schema
ref: string required
time: datetime required
status: enum(pending, started, failed, cancelled, done) required
q: string
```

### Constraints

- `q` is the task of the run once the time started it. The pending times are also kept apart, in the `communications` configuration's `schedule`; cancelling a time takes it off there and leaves its status here as it was.

### Bindings

- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/models/Communication.ts#Communication` — as: model
- provenance: inferred

## Record: Content

### Summary

A content: a named subject and text that automations send.

### Schema

```schema
id: string required unique
name: string
type: string
subject: string
template: string
tag: string
key: string
organisation_id: string ref(juicebar.core#Organisation.id)
```

### Constraints

- The module's contents have a type beginning with `communications`; those it creates are `communications:default`.
- `template` is the text, HTML with placeholders. `tag` is AMG's. `key` names a content another module made for itself.

### Immutable

- `organisation_id`

### Bindings

- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/models/Content.ts#Content` — as: model
- provenance: inferred

## Record: HistoryEntry

### Summary

The record of one run.

### Schema

```schema
id: string required unique
communication_id: string
date: datetime required
user_id: string
organisation_id: string ref(juicebar.core#Organisation.id)
channel: string
subject: string
template: string
recipients: list(part(juicebar.communications#Recipient))
event: string
started: boolean
done: boolean
failed: boolean
error: string
```

### Constraints

- `communication_id` is the automation's id, none for a quick send; the automation may since have been deleted. `user_id` is the staff member's user id; users are not modelled, so it names no Record.
- `event` holds the system event that started the run, with its name and data.

### Bindings

- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/models/CommunicationHistory.ts#CommunicationHistory` — as: model
- provenance: inferred

## Record: TaskQueue

### Summary

The backend's task that carries out one run, with its progress.

### Schema

```schema
id: string required unique
progress: integer min(0) max(100)
done: boolean
failed: boolean
communicationId: string
```

### Bindings

- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/tasking/models/Queue.ts#Queue` — as: model
