## Capability: MessageDelivery

### Summary

The channels configured on the backend, and delivering one message to one address through one of them: by e-mail, push notification or SMS. The e-mail kind is the communications module's own; the others are registered by other modules and the project.

### Operations

- `Channels(name, kind) -> channels`
- `Deliver(channel, address, subject, text, attachments) -> result`

### Bindings

- binds: `service:communication-service#searchChannel` — as: Channels
- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/channels/EmailCommunictionChannel.ts#EmailCommunictionChannel.send` — as: Deliver
- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/channels/PushCommunicationChannel.ts#PushCommunicationChannel.send` — as: Deliver
- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/channels/SMSCommunicationChannel.ts#SMSCommunicationChannel.send` — as: Deliver
- provenance: inferred

## Capability: RecipientProviders

### Summary

The recipient providers registered on the backend under `communications:recipients`: the ones that deliver through a kind of channel, the selection types a provider takes, the customers its parameters reach, and, at a run, the addresses and the placeholder data.

### Operations

- `Providers(kind) -> providers`
- `SelectionTypes(provider) -> selectionTypes`
- `Customers(provider, params, organisation) -> customerIds`
- `Addresses(provider, params, event, organisation) -> addresses`
- `Payload(provider, address, organisation) -> data`

### Bindings

- binds: `service:communication-service#searchRecipients` — as: Providers
- binds: `service:communication-service#getReceiverSupportedSelectionTypes` — as: SelectionTypes
- binds: `service:communication-service#prerenderRecipients` — as: Customers
- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/ICommunicationRecipientProvider.ts#ICommunicationRecipientProvider.getRecipients` — as: Addresses
- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/ICommunicationRecipientProvider.ts#ICommunicationRecipientProvider.getPayload` — as: Payload
- provenance: inferred

## Capability: CustomerDirectory

### Summary

The customers the entities module keeps: searching them, fetching them by id, their groups, the customer attributes the `juicecommerce:entity:attribute` configurations declare, and an attribute's distinct values among the organisation's customers. The entities service answers it and asks for `entities:role`.

### Operations

- `Customers(search, filter, page, pageSize) -> customers`
- `CustomersById(ids, page, pageSize) -> customers`
- `Groups(name, pageSize) -> groups`
- `Attributes() -> attributes`
- `AttributeValues(attribute) -> values`

### Bindings

- binds: `service:entities#fetchEntities` — as: Customers
- binds: `service:entities#fetchEntities` — as: CustomersById
- binds: `service:entities#fetchEntityGroups` — as: Groups
- binds: `service:juicebox:configuration:service#getBySchema` — as: Attributes
- binds: `service:entities#searchAttributeValues` — as: AttributeValues
- provenance: inferred

## Capability: FormCustomers

### Summary

The forms of the forms module and the customers who filled one in, answered by its backend services `ticketing:forms` and `forms:entities`, which ask for `forms:role`.

### Operations

- `Forms(page, pageSize) -> forms`
- `SearchForms(page, pageSize) -> forms`
- `Form(form) -> form`
- `Customers(form, search, page, pageSize) -> customers`

### Bindings

- binds: `service:ticketing:forms#fetch` — as: Forms
- binds: `service:ticketing:forms#search` — as: SearchForms
- binds: `service:ticketing:forms#getForm` — as: Form
- binds: `service:forms:entities#fetch` — as: Customers
- provenance: inferred

